      "question_html": "Simplify. Rewrite with positive exponents only: \\( (2x^2)^3 \\cdot x^{-2} \\)",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "q1",
          "type": "radio",
          "label": "",
          "options": [
            { "value": "A", "text": "\\( 8x^4 \\)" },
            { "value": "B", "text": "\\( 6x^4 \\)" },
            { "value": "C", "text": "\\( 8x^6 \\)" },
            { "value": "D", "text": "\\( 2x^4 \\)" }
          ],
          "answer": "A"
        }
      ],
      "hint": "Power rule first: (ab)^n = a^n * b^n. Then multiply by adding exponents.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "(2x^2)^3 · x^(-2)",
        "= 2^3 · x^6 · x^(-2)          [power rule]",
        "= 8 · x^(6 + (-2))             [product rule: add exponents]",
        "= 8x^4"
      ],
      "feedback_correct": "🔥 Exponent rules applied correctly.",
      "feedback_wrong": "Apply power rule to (2x^2)^3 first: 2^3 = 8, (x^2)^3 = x^6. Then multiply: 8 · x^(6-2) = 8x^4."
    },
